From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexander Astrovsky <astrouski@google.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 21:10:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] eapol_auth: fix PAE state machine transition for PMKSA cache

When a station reconnects or roams using a cached PMKSA entry
(EAPOL_SM_FROM_PMKSA_CACHE), full EAP authentication is bypassed, so
sm->authSuccess and sm->portValid are not set by the EAP state machine.

As a result, in the AUTH_PAE_AUTHENTICATING state, the condition
(sm->authSuccess && sm->portValid) evaluates to false, which can cause
the state machine to either fail to enter AUTH_PAE_AUTHENTICATED or
transition to AUTH_PAE_HELD upon (sm->keyDone && !sm->portValid).

Allow transitioning to AUTH_PAE_AUTHENTICATED when
sm->flags & EAPOL_SM_FROM_PMKSA_CACHE is set, and ensure sm->portValid
is marked true upon entering AUTHENTICATED.

Signed-off-by: Alexander Astrovsky <astrouski@google.com>
---
 src/eapol_auth/eapol_auth_sm.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/src/eapol_auth/eapol_auth_sm.c
+++ b/src/eapol_auth/eapol_auth_sm.c
@@ -315,6 +315,7 @@ SM_STATE(AUTH_PAE, AUTHENTICATED)
 
 	sm->authPortStatus = Authorized;
 	setPortAuthorized();
+	sm->portValid = true;
 	sm->reAuthCount = 0;
 	sm->reAuthenticate = false;
 	if (sm->flags & EAPOL_SM_PREAUTH)
@@ -436,7 +437,8 @@ static void eapol_auth_step_auth_pae(str
 				SM_ENTER(AUTH_PAE, DISCONNECTED);
 			break;
 		case AUTH_PAE_AUTHENTICATING:
-			if (sm->authSuccess && sm->portValid)
+			if ((sm->authSuccess && sm->portValid) ||
+			    (sm->flags & EAPOL_SM_FROM_PMKSA_CACHE))
 				SM_ENTER(AUTH_PAE, AUTHENTICATED);
 			else if (sm->authFail ||
 				 (sm->keyDone && !sm->portValid))
